course: dictionary
lesson: 4221
title: Gradually: little by little
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gradually means slowly, a little at a time, over a period. It is the opposite of suddenly, which means all at once. When you see gradually, ask yourself: did this change happen in small steps over time?
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Gradually she began to feel better» tells you the feeling came back slowly, not in one moment. Ice that gradually melts does not turn to water in a second; it gets smaller bit by bit as it warms.
explain: Gradually shows up in science, maths and stories. In maths, a line that rises gradually has a gentle slope. A plant grows gradually, and your fitness builds up gradually when you exercise. Swap in «little by little» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Gradually means slowly, a little at a time, over a period.
fact: Suddenly is the opposite of gradually: it means all at once, without warning.
fact: «Gradually» often describes change over time, such as ice gradually melting or the sky gradually getting dark.
fact: In maths, a number that gradually increases goes up in small steps.
fact: «A cool-down of slow movement after exercise helps the body calm down gradually.»
exercise: «The ice on the pond gradually melted as the sun got warmer.» What does gradually mean here? | Backwards | Suddenly, in one moment | Loudly | *Slowly, a little at a time
exercise: Which word is the opposite of gradually? | softly | *suddenly | slowly | steadily
exercise: «Gradually she began to feel better.» What does gradually tell us about how she began to feel better? | Only once | All at once, overnight | *Little by little, over time | Not at all
test:
«The hill rose gradually, so the walk was never too steep.» What does gradually describe? | *A slow, gentle rise over a distance | A sudden drop | A loud noise | Going round in circles
Which sentence uses gradually correctly? | The lights went off gradually, with a bang | *The sky gradually got darker as the evening went on | He gradually shouted at once | The plate gradually smashed in one moment
exam:
Which phrase is closest in meaning to gradually? | *Little by little | In a flash | Right now | Without warning
